[1.045, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[6A\t\t  \u001b[90mGemini 4 Argon (Medium)\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[23D\u001b[90m~/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla\u001b[m\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[42C\u001b[2mGemini 4 Argon · medium\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.909, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[90mAuto mode: edits & safe commands auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[21C\u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · \u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[95D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.0, "m", "1. Ready for Initial Prompt"]
[1.0, "o", "\u001b[?2026hI want to build an out-of-tree Apache NuttX application and custom board configuration in a new\r\n  `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` directory of this workspace for a Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 mounted on a breadboard with 1\u001b[K\r\n  potentiometer and 6 discrete LEDs acting as a bar graph.\u001b[K\r\n\n  Requirements:\r\n  - Keep `nuttx/` and `apps/` submodules completely unmodified (integrate out-of-tree).\r\n  - Read the potentiometer via ADC and drive the 6 breadboard LEDs as a bar graph.\r\n  - Provide an interactive NuttShell (`nsh>`) console over the USB-C port, while auto-starting the bar-graph\r\n  application automatically at boot even before USB serial attaches.\r\n  - Include a Makefile in `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` that builds host unit tests (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph test`)\r\n  and compiles the firmware into `nuttx/nuttx.uf2` (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph`).\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.001, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90C\u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · Gemini 4 Argon · medium\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[84C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.0, "m", "2. Initial Prompt: XIAO RP2350 Bar Graph"]
[0.2, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[7A\u001b[J\u001b[3A\u001b[2C\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[89C\u001b[1K \u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · Gemini 4 Argon · medium\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\n\u001b[90m? for shortcuts\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[13D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001bM\u001b[58C\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> I want to build an out-of-tree Apache NuttX application and custom board configuration in a new\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` directory of this workspace for a Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 mounted on a breadboard with 1\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m  potentiometer and 6 discrete LEDs acting as a bar graph.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m  \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  Requirements:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Keep `nuttx/` and `apps/` submodules completely unmodified (integrate out-of-tree).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Read the potentiometer via ADC and drive the 6 breadboard LEDs as a bar graph.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Provide an interactive NuttShell (`nsh>`) console over the USB-C port, while auto-starting the bar-graph\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  application automatically at boot even before USB serial attaches.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Include a Makefile in `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` that builds host unit tests (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph test`) and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  compiles the firmware into `nuttx/nuttx.uf2` (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph`).\u001b[m\r\n⣷  \u001b[90mGenera\u001b[94mting.\u001b[90m..\u001b["]
[0.0, "o", "m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[77X\u001b[77C\u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · Gemini 4 Argon · medium\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
