[0.066, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[32A\u001b[1;34m> I want to build an out-of-tree Apache NuttX application and custom board configuration in a new\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[34;1m  `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` directory of this workspace for a Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 mounted on a breadboard with 1\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  potentiometer and 6 discrete LEDs acting as a bar graph.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  Requirements:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Keep `nuttx/` and `apps/` submodules completely unmodified (integrate out-of-tree).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Read the potentiometer via ADC and drive the 6 breadboard LEDs as a bar graph.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Provide an interactive NuttShell (`nsh>`) console over the USB-C port, while auto-starting the bar-graph\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  application automatically at boot even before USB serial attaches.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Include a Makefile in `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` that builds host unit tests (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph test`) and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  compiles the firmware into `nuttx/nuttx.uf2` (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph`).\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 7.4s\u001b["]
[0.0, "o", "m \u001b[37m(Examining the workspace files to understand the repository structure. Starting to review existi...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(board.h)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 19s, 196 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Which XIAO RP2350 pins are connected to the potentiometer and the 6 LEDs (in order from lowest to highest on the\r\n  bar graph), and are the LEDs wired active-high or active-low?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> any free breadboard pins you pick are fine, you are free to design the board as appropriate\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 16m 20s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The Makefile's `configure:` target needs an update. If the board's defconfig and the NuttX d...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ls -la /Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla /Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla/nut...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m"]
