[0.099, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[32A\u001b[1;34m  - Keep `nuttx/` and `apps/` submodules completely unmodified (integrate out-of-tree).\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[34;1m  - Read the potentiometer via ADC and drive the 6 breadboard LEDs as a bar graph.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Provide an interactive NuttShell (`nsh>`) console over the USB-C port, while auto-starting the bar-graph\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  application automatically at boot even before USB serial attaches.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  - Include a Makefile in `xiao-rp2350-bargraph/` that builds host unit tests (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph test`) and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  compiles the firmware into `nuttx/nuttx.uf2` (`make -C xiao-rp2350-bargraph`).\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 7.4s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Examining the workspace files to understand the repository structure. Starting to review existi...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(board.h)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 19s, 196 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Which XIAO RP2350 pins are connected to the potentiometer and the 6 LEDs (in order from lowest to highest "]
