[0.051, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[33A\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 19s, 196 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  Which XIAO RP2350 pins are connected to the potentiometer and the 6 LEDs (in order from lowest to highest on the\r\n  bar graph), and are the LEDs wired active-high or active-low?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> any free breadboard pins you pick are fine, you are free to design the board as appropriate\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 16m 20s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The Makefile's `configure:` target needs an update. If the board's defconfig and the NuttX d...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ls -la /Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla /Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla/nut\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 10 files \u001b[37m(board.h, rp23xx_bringup.c, rp23xx_userleds.c, +7)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m… 106 more actions (52 reads, 26 edits, 28 commands: 1 failed) …\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b["]
[0.0, "o", "m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 3 files \u001b[37m(defconfig, defconfig, Makefile)\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[47D\u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(make -C /Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla/xiao-rp2350-bargraph -j4)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  Rebuilding the NuttX firmware with \u001b[94mCONFIG_ANALOG=y\u001b[m enabled so the RP2350 ADC driver and \u001b[94mbargraph\u001b[m application are\r\n  registered and linked; waiting for the build to complete.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m 2 commands \u001b[37m(arm-none-eabi-nm /Us... · make -C /Users/brett...)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  The out-of-tree Apache NuttX application and custom Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 board configuration have been\r\n  implemented in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc6fbfe35ffafc51f;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-vanilla/xiao-rp2350-bargraph/README.md\u0007xiao-rp2350-bargraph/\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1m### Breadboard Pinout (Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  All 6 bar-graph LEDs are placed on non-ADC digital pins (\u001b[94mD3\u001b[m–\u001b[94mD8\u001b[m) because \u001b[94mrp23xx_adc.c\u001b[m resets \u001b[94mGPIO2"]
[0.0, "o", "6\u001b[m–\u001b[94mGPIO29\u001b[m (\u001b[94mD0\u001b[m–\u001b[94mD2\u001b[m)\r\n  to analog mode (\u001b[94mRP23XX_GPIO_FUNC_NULL\u001b[m) when initializing the ADC peripheral:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n   Function\u001b[19X\u001b[19C│ XIAO Pad\u001b[19X\u001b[19C│ RP2350 GPIO\u001b[16X\t\t│ Active Polarity / Notes\r\n  ────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────\r\n   \u001b[1mPotentiometer Wiper\u001b[m** \u001b[5b│\u001b[28X\u001b[28C│\u001b[28X\t\t\t\t│\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[87D\u001b[?2026l"]
